@startuml codeemb-graphcodebert
' GraphCodeBERT's two input channels. The token channel (green) is wired in
' libgrammstein. The data-flow channel (muted, dashed) is what the paper adds and
' is NOT wired: `use_data_flow` is never read and no DFG tensor is ever built.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-graphcodebert.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/graphcodebert.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #263238
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title GraphCodeBERT — token channel (wired) ⊕ data-flow channel (NOT wired)

rectangle "**source code c**" as src #EF6C00

package "Token channel — wired in GraphCodeBertEmbedder" {
  rectangle "**Tokenizer**\nencode(c, true), truncate to 512" as tok #EF6C00
  rectangle "**input_ids**  ·  **attention_mask**" as ids #2E7D32
  rectangle "**position_ids** = 0‥L−1\nsupplied **iff** the graph declares\nan input whose name contains it" as pos #43A047
}

package "Data-flow channel — described by Guo et al. 2021, NOT built here" {
  rectangle "**Parse → AST**" as ast #90A4AE
  rectangle "**Data-flow graph** 𝒢 = (V, E)\nV = variable occurrences\n(vᵢ, vⱼ) ∈ E ⟺ value of vᵢ comes from vⱼ" as dfg #90A4AE
  rectangle "**Graph-guided masked attention**\nMᵢⱼ = 0 if edge/alignment, −∞ otherwise" as mask #90A4AE
}

rectangle "**ONNX RoBERTa encoder**\n125M params · d = 768" as enc #2E7D32
rectangle "**CLS pooling** → **L2 normalize**\n**v̂ ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸**" as out #455A64

src --> tok
tok --> ids
tok --> pos
ids --> enc
pos --> enc
enc --> out

src -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> ast
ast -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> dfg
dfg -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> mask
mask -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> enc : **never reaches the session**

note bottom of dfg #ECEFF1
  ""GraphCodeBertConfig::use_data_flow"" exists,
  defaults to **false**, and is **never read**.
  No DFG tensor is constructed and no graph-guided
  mask is applied — you inherit only the structural
  inductive bias baked into the pre-trained weights.
end note

note right of out #E8F5E9
  libgrammstein //does// build data-flow edges —
  DfgRead / DfgWrite / DfgFlow / DfgDepends in
  the Code Property Graph (src/code/cpg.rs).
  They are simply not fed to this encoder.
end note

@enduml
